[{"id":94111,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94111\">#1</a> I see there’s a conference coming up <a href=\"http://indico.ictp.it/event/9639\">Generalized Cohomology and Physics</a>.  EDIT: Link corrected as per #3 (and #5).</p>","timestamp":1632556677,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":94112,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94112\">#2</a> By the way, I came across your essay, Urs, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/The+use+of+nonabelian+differential+cohomology\">The use of nonabelian differential cohomology</a>. Perhaps worth an indication of what has come to be seen post-2012?</p>","timestamp":1632557026,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":94114,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94114\">#3</a> The link in your <a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94111\">#1</a> is probably meant to be <a href=\"http://indico.ictp.it/event/9639\">indico.ictp.it/event/9639</a>.</p>\n<p>Regarding <a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94112\">#2</a>: The latest exposition of non-abelian differential cohomology and physics we have is the Introduction to <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/The%20Character%20Map%20in%20Twisted%20Non-Abelian%20Cohomology\">The character map in (twisted differential) non-abelian cohomology</a></em>.</p>","timestamp":1632557677,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":94115,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94115\">#4</a> Yes, sorry, that link.</p>\n<p>Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94112\">#2</a>, I just meant you might consider adding a mention on that page to a later exposition, as in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94114\">#3</a>. I was just looking about to see how commonly the physics-cohomology connection is made, and was sent to your 2012 essay. </p>\n<p>I have yet to see any trace of any philosopher of physics writing on cohomology.</p>","timestamp":1632563215,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":94128,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94128\">#5</a> The link is still broken!</p>","timestamp":1632607653,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":94133,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Generalized.20Cohomology.20and.20Physics.20conference/near/94133\">#6</a> It’s almost as though I don’t want people to find it.</p>","timestamp":1632639115,"subject":"Generalized Cohomology and Physics conference","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]